{
  "full_prompt_html": "<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Act as a senior account executive, a sales operations manager and a deal qualification coach.</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Turn my notes from a discovery call into a deal summary our team can act on. [Paste your call notes, the transcript or the Teams meeting recap.] [Paste the account name, the product or service discussed, and the CRM fields your team must complete.]</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Structure the summary in four parts:</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>1. What the Client Said</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSummarize the client’s business problem in their own words, with direct quotes from the notes where possible.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDescribe the process or tool they use today and what it costs them in time, money or risk.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nIdentify the trigger: why they are looking now.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>2. Qualification</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nAssess the deal against budget, authority, need, timeline and decision process. For each one, state what we know, the evidence, and what is still unknown.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nName every person mentioned, their role, and whether they are a decision-maker, an influencer or a user.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nRate the deal as qualified, partly qualified or not qualified, and give the reason in one sentence.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>3. Gaps and Risks</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nList the questions we did not ask and must ask on the next call.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nFlag any warning signs, such as no clear owner, no budget, or a competitor already in place.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>4. Next Steps</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nPropose the next meeting, who should attend from both sides, and its goal.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDraft a short follow-up email to the client that restates their problem and confirms the next step.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Deliver the summary as short sections with bullet points, followed by the CRM fields as a two-column table and the follow-up email. Do not add facts that are not in the notes, and mark anything you infer.</span></p>",
  "n": 5,
  "subject_area": "Sales operations",
  "summary": "Summarize discovery call notes into the client’s problem, qualification against budget, authority, need and timeline, open questions, risks, and next steps.",
  "title": "Turn discovery call notes into a qualified deal summary"
}
